# Historical findings in commit 9e5233ca, which added the release-0.1
# implementation plan. All seven are the same illustrative test fixture,
# `0123456789abcdef`, appearing in example code inside a planning document. It
# was never a credential; the fixture was later renamed to carry the explicit
# `not-a-real-secret-` marker that `.gitleaks.toml` allowlists.
#
# Fingerprint-based exemptions are normally the wrong tool, because they key on
# `commit:file:rule:line` and stop matching when lines move — an exemption that
# drifts off its target, or worse onto a real secret that later lands at that
# line. That objection does not apply here: these fingerprints are pinned to a
# commit that is already merged and immutable, so they cannot drift. Current and
# future code is covered by the marker convention in `.gitleaks.toml` instead.
#
# Do not add entries here for anything in the working tree. If a new finding
# appears, either it is a real secret or the fixture needs the marker.
